  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member scanning my flags, I want the unread-pages number on topic rows to be readable at a glance, so that the capsule #590 brought back does its job.\n\nRefs #590 (found in its Mac check; build `cb3da9ce` = `origin/dev-swift`).\n\n### Observed\niPhone 18 Pro and iPad Pro 13\" simulators (iOS 27.0), Favoris and Catégories > Apple lists. The capsule is the app accent (a light cyan) with white bold caption2 text. Measured on the screenshots (fill sampled, WCAG contrast with white):\n\n| Appearance | Capsule fill | White text contrast |\n|---|---|---|\n| Light | (89, 227, 255) | 1.52 : 1 |\n| Light + Increase Contrast | (89, 227, 255) | 1.52 : 1 |\n| Dark | (73, 214, 242) | 1.72 : 1 |\n| Dark + Increase Contrast | (73, 214, 242) | 1.72 : 1 |\n\nWCAG asks 4.5 : 1 for text this size (3 : 1 even for large text). Increase Contrast changes nothing.\n\nLegacy (`Common.swift:691-700, 3122-3130` @ 2440d79) used a grey capsule with white text in light (`.secondary`) and a white capsule with black text in dark.\n\nRelated, same pattern: the MP list \"non lu\" capsule at half strength (member has read) is white on (198, 198, 201) in light, 1.70 : 1 (#617 covers Increase Contrast in dark only).\n\n### Acceptance\n- The unread-pages capsule reaches at least 4.5 : 1 in light, dark and with Increase Contrast (for example legacy's colours, or a darker fill), checked on the Mac.\n- Same check for the MP \"non lu\" capsule at half strength in light, or a note on #617.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
